  "title": "Erdős Problem #866",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $k\\geq 3$ and $g_k(N)$ be minimal such that if $A\\subseteq \\{1,\\ldots,2N\\}$ has $\\lvert A\\rvert \\geq N+g_k(N)$ then there exist integers $b_1,\\ldots,b_k$ such that all $\\binom{k}{2}$ pairwise sums are in $A$ (but the $b_i$ themselves need not be in $A$).\nEstimate $g_k(N)$.",
